  <section class="simteaser" id="simulator" aria-labelledby="simt-h">
    <div class="wrap simt-in">
      <div>
        <h2 id="simt-h" class="h-head">Your bill after solar,<br>simulated.</h2>
        <p class="lede-d">Most solar quotes multiply your bill by a saving percentage. The Eternalgy Solar Simulator, built in-house by our software team, rebuilds your TNB bill from the tariff, follows every kilowatt-hour your system generates, and calculates the bill you will pay after solar, item by item. For homes and for businesses.</p>
        <ul class="simt-steps">
          <li><b>Your bill</b> The amount and month on your TNB bill.</li>
          <li><b>Tariff match</b> The usage that produces that bill, with that month's surcharge.</li>
          <li><b>System size</b> Panels sized to your usage at Malaysian sun-peak hours.</li>
          <li><b>Energy flow</b> Used on site, exported, or beyond the credit cap.</li>
          <li><b>New bill</b> Every component recalculated at your new usage.</li>
          <li><b>Your saving</b> Old bill minus new bill, plus the export credit.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="acts"><a class="btn btn--light" href="https://wa.me/601121000099?text=Hi%20Eternalgy%2C%20please%20simulate%20my%20TNB%20bill%20after%20solar." target="_blank" rel="noopener">Send us your bill</a><a class="tlink" href="/docs/eternalgy-corporate-profile-2026.pdf#page=5" target="_blank" rel="noopener">How the simulator works (PDF)</a></div>
      </div>
      <div class="simt-ex">
        <div class="ex"><p class="ex-k">Home · RM500 bill, April 2026, three-phase</p><p class="ex-n">RM361.58</p><p class="ex-s">saved a month · RM504.67 → RM143.09 · 10.4 kWp, 16 × 650 W panels</p></div>
        <div class="ex"><p class="ex-k">Business · RM5,000 bill, low-voltage commercial, open daily 8 am–6 pm</p><p class="ex-n">RM2,387.14</p><p class="ex-s">saved a month · RM4,999.68 → RM2,612.54 · 45.5 kWp, 70 × 650 W panels</p></div>
        <p class="ex-note">Worked examples from the Eternalgy Solar Simulator, TNB tariff in force October 2026. A simulation cannot know weather, shading, changes in usage or future tariffs; we confirm it with a site survey and, ideally, up to twelve months of bills before you commit.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

